     "result_text_tail": "del simplifications:**\n  - One-time costs are counted in the year they occur.\n  - Japan has no working-capital input in the pack.\n  - Tax and exchange-rate effects are excluded.\n  - The tariff rise and ad cost are run as scenarios.\n\n**Checks**\n- **Sources:** all 378 numbers trace to the briefing pack or to calculations from it, and there are no placeholders. Each calculation is a live formula in the workbook.\n- **Independent check:** a second reviewer rebuilt the cash model and found no numeric errors. Five of its wording points were valid and I fixed them, for example \"never pays back\" became \"has not paid back by 2030\".\n- **QA script:** no failures and no layout warnings. Four minor warnings remain, which I judged acceptable:\n  - Three sidebar numbers explain a chart rather than being computed from it.\n  - The US market-size question is something Onsoo can't influence. I kept it because the go/no-go depends on it.\n- **Not possible here:** re-opening web sources and a second independent source per number. The pack is the only source.\n- **Not viewed:** I couldn't look at the slides as images in this environment, so the layout checks are the renderer's automated ones.\n\nOf the tree's 13 hypotheses, 5 were confirmed, 3 revised and 5 refuted.\n\nThe generator scripts and the deck spec are in `./build/`. From there I can switch the theme or re-run the case if the tariff decision or the inputs change.\n\nFiles are in `./deliverable/`:\n- onsoo-us-entry.pptx\n- onsoo-us-entry-sources.xlsx"
